From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stoiko Ivanov <s.ivanov@proxmox.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:18:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] scripts/make_gitrev.sh: prefer version from d/changelog

make_gitrev.sh is called by make to create zfs_gitrev.h, which is
used to identify the source-version of a build in the sysctl
`kernel.spl.gitrev`. I noticed the discrepancy between kernel's
build via `sbuild` (kernel.spl.gitrev = unknown) or directly
(kernel.spl.gitrev looks like zfs-2.4.4-0-g71a9f95786).

afaict the issue is purely cosmetic, and I ran into while comparing
sysctl output of 2 kernels.

make_gitrev.sh relies on having a .git for finding the information,
which is available (as pointer to the submodule) in a checkout of
pve-kernel, but not in the source-package used by sbuild.

creating the file and commiting it to the source-package would be an
alternative - but having the version from d/changelog conveys the
same information for our released kernels.

keeping the fallback to the git revision for direct builds which don't
have debian/ copied inside.

Signed-off-by: Stoiko Ivanov <s.ivanov@proxmox.com>
---
 scripts/make_gitrev.sh | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/make_gitrev.sh b/scripts/make_gitrev.sh
index f85c9db097f0049bc83d06c988085b9f446df892..2b50cf4bcb9d414892fe958199a5032b563912ab 100755
--- a/scripts/make_gitrev.sh
+++ b/scripts/make_gitrev.sh
@@ -50,8 +50,10 @@ case "${GITREV}" in
 	*) ;;
 esac
 
+# prefer the version from debian/changelog for our in-kernel builds
 ZFS_GITREV=$({ cd "${top_srcdir}" &&
-	git describe --always --long --dirty 2>/dev/null; } || :)
+	dpkg-parsechangelog -S Version 2>/dev/null ||
+	git describe --always --long --dirty 2>/dev/null;} ||:)
 
 if [ -z "${ZFS_GITREV}" ]
 then
